## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region, auditable JIT access with strict policy enforcement and lifecycle controls in SAP-heavy AWS environments.

## Key Concepts

- Cross‑region IAM role trust and STS AssumeRole
- SCPs and least privilege mapping for SAP actions
- VPC Endpoints for SAP components and private networking
- JIT elevation TTL and automated revocation via Step Functions
- Central policy store and audit trail (CloudTrail, Config)

## Code Example

```hcl
# Terraform snippet: cross-account role and SCP (illustrative)
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_operator_cross_account" {
  name = "sap-operator-cross-account"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::<OPERATOR_ACCOUNT_ID>:root" }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      Condition = { StringEquals = { "sts:ExternalId" = "SAP_OPS" } }
    }]
  })
  tags = { ManagedBy = "OpenCode" }
}

resource "aws_organizations_policy" "sap_jit_scp" {
  name        = "SAP-JIT-SCP"
  description = "Limit actions to SAP-related AWS permissions"
  content     = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["ec2:Describe*","s3:Get*","logs:CreateLogStream","logs:PutLogEvents"], Resource = "*" }
    ]
  })
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test cross-region authorization sync and revocation at scale?
- What metrics and alarms would validate the JIT lifecycle and policy compliance?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of AWS patching automation, SAP patching options, health checks, rollback strategies, and CloudFormation for operational guardrails.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Maintenance Windows
- SAP patching options: SUM vs OS patches
- Pre/post patch validation: SAPControl, SAP background jobs, host metrics
- Rollback strategies: SAP backups, AMI snapshots
- CloudFormation for roles and patch baselines

## Code Example
```javascript
// CFN skeleton (pseudo)
{
  "AWSTemplateFormatVersion": "2010-09-09",
  "Resources": {
    "SAPSSMRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": { "Version": "2012-10-17", "Statement": [ { "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": { "Service": ["ec2.amazonaws.com", "ssm.amazonaws.com"] }, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole" } ] },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": [ "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMFullAccess" ]
      }
    },
    "SAPPatchBaseline": {
      "Type": "AWS::SSM::PatchBaseline",
      "Properties": {
        "Name": "SAPBaseline",
        "OperatingSystem": "AmazonLinux2"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify patch success in SAP and the OS without impacting production?
- How would you extend to multi-region DR alignment and scoped approvals?

## Why This Is Asked
